  "finding": {
    "id": "CLOCK_RUNTIME_NULL_PRIMARY_M1",
    "severity": "Source HOLD before runtime",
    "bodyLocations": [
      "body.mjs:29,44,46 prepareMapped",
      "body.mjs:69,75,76 runJcoWorker",
      "body.mjs:82,101,102 runDifferential"
    ],
    "entryLocations": [
      "entry.mjs:96,105 authenticate",
      "entry.mjs:108,112 prepare"
    ],
    "evidence": "Pure extracted capturedRun stores an exact raw kind:throw/null and rethrows null. The three body catches then store primary=null, indistinguishable from their initial sentinel, so primary!==null is false. A fresh one-call worker can label completion even though its retained record is a throw. Two entry combined-failure catches also omit a caught null from their AggregateError.",
    "boundary": "The full parent independently validates kind:return/type:string and all expected raw counts, so it rejects this raw throw. Mapping normally still fails on its absent mapping-result file. No false full differential PASS or observed target failure is claimed; ordinary Wasm traps are expected RuntimeError objects. The bug is a Source-level child/phase failure-state inconsistency.",
    "correction": {
      "path": "/Users/dan/dev/StarlingMonkey/tests/node-compat/foundation-scheduler/independent-clock-v13-runtime-source-review-v1/required-correction-contract.json",
      "sha256": "660b2fa1c41a1eb8e2e14d95343a4c9749cb75dc0eae39f1d906a649a763a7a3",
      "bytes": 1744
    }
  },
